      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "Public domain",
      "artist": "USDAgov",
      "description": "Pamlico Rose Institute Executive Director Robert Sand at the PRI's The Barn on February 15, 2024, in Washington, North Carolina - With the assistance of a $113 thousand USDA Rural Development Community Facilities Grant, The Pamlico Rose Institute is helping female Veterans by promoting wellness and building resilience through their various programs, activities and events. Rural Development’s investment was used to restore The Barn. This structure is being used for community events and workshops including woodworking, visual arts, crafts and yoga classes. “Our healing programs do not meet their full potential without The Barn,” said Sands. “The Barn opens up the number of Veterans we can serve and expands the types of art media we can provide for women Veterans and the community.”\nFor more information about The Barn please see pamlicorose.org/barn/\nFor more information about USDA's Community Facilities Programs please see rd.usda.gov/programs-services/community-facilities\n\nUSDA Media by Robert Kerns.",
